max stores the maximum subarray sum ending at the current index.
ans stores the maximum subarray sum found so far.

For every element, I calculate two possibilities:
v1 = max + nums[i]: Extend the previous subarray by adding the current element.
v2 = nums[i]: Start a new subarray from the current element.
I update max by choosing the larger of these two values, then update ans if the current maximum is greater than the best answer found so far.

I initialize both variables with nums[0] so the solution also works when all the elements are negative.


class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int n=nums.length;
        int max=nums[0],ans=nums[0];

        for(int i=1;i<n;i++){
            int v1=max+nums[i];
            int v2=nums[i];

            max=Math.max(v1,v2);
            ans=Math.max(ans,max);
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
